    {
      "id": "p0210-b018",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Because knock-knock jokes don't exist in Japan, and because the English joke in this scene plays with how \"this is\" and \"dishes\" are pronounced, the scene would've made little sense in a literal translation. To get around this problem, the translator replaced the knock-knock joke with a joke related to two common forms of Japanese comedy: solo acts and duo manzai acts.",
        "raw": "Because knock-knock jokes don't exist in Japan, and because the English joke\nin this scene plays with how \"this is\" and \"dishes\" are pronounced, the scene\nwould've made little sense in a literal translation. To get around this problem,\nthe translator replaced the knock-knock joke with a joke related to two\ncommon forms of Japanese comedy: solo acts and duo manzai acts.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.2995588,
          0.73177857,
          0.8938714,
          0.81746429
